      5 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تبصّل</span></b>  <i>It</i> (a thing) <i>was,</i> or <i>became, several
fold,</i> or <i>many fold, like the coats of the</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَصَل</span> [or
<i>onion</i>]. (Z, TA.) See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُتَبّصِّلٌ</span>. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  It is also
trans.: see 2, in two places. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  [Hence,] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَبَصَّلُوهُ</span>
(assumed tropical:)  <i>They begged of him so much that all that he had
became exhausted.</i> (Sgh, K.)

